WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.580
On November 14th 2017, Zimbabwe military troops drove tanks into the capital city, Harare.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.580
"Military police on tank, this is happening in Harare. "

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.800
"Wow! It's real guys, it is real."

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.650
They patrolled the streets, blocked access
to government buildings, and took over the

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.749
state television station to insist….

00:00:17.749 --> 00:00:20.600
This is not a military takeover of government.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.710
But it clearly was.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.550
Troops invaded the presidential palace and put the president, Robert Mugabe in custody.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:36.250
“...Comrade Robert Mugabe, and his family are safe and sound, and their security is guaranteed."

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.030
When you hear that a military coup has happened,
it’s common to assume that the result is

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.010
a transfer of power…

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.920
But in this case... it’s clear there is
no revolution.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.760
It’s merely an internal fight among the
country’s elites.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.309
Zimbabwe is one of the most corrupt countries
in the world; and what we’re seeing is a

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:53.850
fight to keep it that way...

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:59.600
As soon as we have accomplished our mission,
we expect that the situation will return to

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.600
normalcy."

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.380
Once praised as a war hero, Robert Mugabe
helped Zimbabwe win independence from Great

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.380
Britain in 1980.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.200
He became president under Zimbabwe’s new
constitution with the wide support of the people.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.770
But soon, he digressed into a repressive dictator

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:19.280
He secured his power through aggression and
threats, there have been reports of state-sponsored

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.500
torture and killings.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:27.140
Now that Mugabe is 93 years old, and reportedly
in poor health, the fight for political influence

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:28.630
is more intense than ever.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.659
And it’s caused a split in Mugabe’s own
party, the ZANU-PF.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:37.680
On one side we have the old guard lead by
Mugabe’s sacked vice-president Emmerson

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.680
Mnangagwa.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.829
Like Mugabe, he fought for Zimbabwe’s independence
and has a checkered past that includes human

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:46.880
rights abuses against political opponents
and ethnic minorities.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.490
As an old friend of Mugabe’s and vice president
since 2014, Mnangagwa was the heir-apparent

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.490
for many years.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:59.280
But that all changed on November 6th when
Mugabe’s government said Mnangagwa had exhibited

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.009
“traits of disloyalty” and fired him.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.820
This seemed to indicate Mugabe’s support
for another successor; Grace Mugabe his own

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.030
wife.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.390
She has recently risen within the party, but
is extremely unpopular nationwide, mostly

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.860
due to her expensive shopping habits, which
earned her the nickname, Gucci Grace.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.911
The military has sided with Mnangagwa.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:24.600
"that when it comes to matters
of protecting our revolution, the military

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.430
will not hesitate to step in."

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.830
On November 15th they did just that, taking
control of the capital in what they deemed

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:35.280
“a guardian coup”; to protecting the Zimbabwe
people and “democracy”.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.590
But their interests are more self-motivated;
they want to secure their own power.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:44.210
They have control over lucrative farm and
mining operations and access to foreign currency.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:49.330
To keep this power, they need a united ZANU-PF,
who face elections scheduled for 2018.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:52.060
What’s missing in all this?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.640
The people of Zimbabwe.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.380
Whoever ends up in charge…

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.810
Mnangagwa, the military, or Grace Mugabe ….

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.670
corruption will continue.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.840
All these actors are want to keep the status
quo.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.480
But for the general population; the status quo is a destroyed economy.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.580
the status quo is a society of unequal opportunity.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.290
During Mugabe’s 37 years of leadership,
massive corruption was commonplace.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.881
There have been repeated allegations of Mugabe and his cabinet embezzling money from

00:03:16.881 --> 00:03:19.260
mining and diamond industries.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.050
Mugabe even won the “state owned” lottery
in 2000.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:28.200
Transparency International estimates that
Zimbabwe loses $1billion per year to corruption.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.940
All the while Zimbabwe’s economy suffered.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.510
The poverty rate is at 72%.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.760
Inflation has reached peaks of 231,000,000%
!!!!! ….

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.750
With GDP growth, stagnant.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.730
This has made Zimbabwe one of the most economically
unequal countries in the world.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.060
A problem it shares with much of the region.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:52.540
Studies show that “low levels of economic
growth and high levels of poverty are common

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.040
conditions in African countries that experience military coups.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.780
In fact, 36% of all coup attempts since 1950
have occurred in Africa.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.180
The problem is coups rarely address these
problems.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.420
Military coups in Niger (2010), Burkina Faso
(2014) and Burundi (2015) were attempts by

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.590
leaders to extend their term limits.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.660
While coups in Guinea (2008) and Togo (2005)
were sparked by competition over succession.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.800
The same appears to be happening in Zimbabwe,

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.060
What's uncertain in the near future is Zimbabwe's political leadership.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.260
What's certain is that politicians fight over their own self-interests and those of the people are forgotten.

